## 3. Data Cleaning Rules

**No record is dropped silently.** Every rejected row is written to the quarantine with its `batch_id`, `rule_id`, and reason (Section 9) and is counted in the metadata (Section 8). A record that is cleaned and kept is *modified*, not rejected.

### 3.1 Rules

| Rule ID | Target | Condition | Action | Justification |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| C-01 | All text columns | Leading, trailing, or repeated spaces | Trim and collapse to single spaces (`description` is trimmed only) | Avoids false mismatches in comparisons and duplicate detection |
| C-02 | All columns | Blank, `nan`, `none`, or `null` | Convert to missing | One definition of "missing" |
| C-03 | `sales.customer_name`, `shop_name`, `phone_number` | Missing | Fill `Unknown` | The sale and its money values are still valid |
| C-04 | `expenses.description` | Missing | Fill `No description` | The expense amount is still valid |
| C-05 | Required columns (note 1) | Missing | **Reject** | Keys, money, and dates are never invented |
| C-06 | `quantity`, `unit_price`, `amount` | Zero or negative | **Reject** | Invalid business value |
| C-07 | All business columns of a table | Identical after cleaning (note 2) | Keep the first in file order; reject the rest | The copies are identical, so keeping any one is correct |
| C-08 | `recorded_by`, `sales.stock_id` | Key has no parent (note 3) | **Reject** | The Load stage would reject the row anyway; prevents broken links |

**Notes**

1. **C-05 required columns:** all columns in the Section 6 contract except the three that C-03 and C-04 fill. Primary keys are checked only when present.
2. **C-07 comparison:** all business columns except the optional primary key. Extraction already stops repeated keys, so these copies carry different IDs or none. Dropped rows go to the quarantine and are counted as `duplicates_dropped`.
3. **C-08 parents:** `recorded_by` must be in `users.user_id`. `sales.stock_id` must be in `stocks.stock_id` of the database or of this batch. When the lookup is unavailable the check is skipped and logged (V-06 `SKIPPED`).

### 3.2 Execution Order

1. C-01 text cleanup, then C-02 missing-value normalization
2. Type conversion and standardization (S-01 to S-06); a failed conversion rejects the row
3. C-03 and C-04 fills, then C-05 required-value rejects
4. C-06 invalid values, then C-08 orphan check
5. C-07 duplicate removal
6. B-01 derivation (Section 5)

A row rejected at an earlier step is not processed by later steps and is counted once, under the first rule that rejected it.

### 3.3 Required Considerations: Where Each Is Handled

| Consideration | Rule(s) |
|---|---|
| Missing or null values (default, fill, or reject) | C-02, C-05 (reject), C-03, C-04 (fill) |
| Duplicates and which record is kept | C-07 (first kept) |
| Whitespace and invalid characters | C-01, S-06 |
| Invalid and out-of-range values | S-01 to S-03 (failed conversion), C-06 |
| Orphan records | C-08 |

