## 4. Standardization and Data Type Rules

All values arrive as text. A value that cannot be converted is **never guessed**; the row is rejected under its S rule.

### 4.1 Data Types and Formats

| Rule ID | Columns | Standard format / type | On failure |
|---|---|---|---|
| S-01 | `updated_at`, `sale_date`, `expense_date` | DATETIME `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` | Reject and log |
| S-02 | `quantity`, `recorded_by`, `stock_id`, key columns | INTEGER | Reject and log (e.g. `100.5`, `abc`) |
| S-03 | `unit_price`, `amount`, `total_amount` | DECIMAL(12,2) | Reject and log |
| S-04 | `size`, `unit` | Upper case (`CHB-4`), lower case (`pcs`) | Cannot fail |
| S-05 | `customer_name`, `shop_name`, `category` | Title Case | Cannot fail |
| S-06 | `phone_number` | Digits only, kept as text so the leading 0 stays | A value with no digits is treated as missing and filled by C-03 |

`description` is TEXT, trimmed only, casing kept.

**Conversion details**

- **S-01 dates:** accepted source formats include `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]`, and `MM/DD/YYYY [h:mm AM/PM]`. A date without a time becomes `00:00:00`. Time zone is Asia/Manila; an offset in the source is dropped and the clock time kept.
- **S-02 whole numbers:** thousands separators are removed. `350.0` becomes `350`; `100.5` is not whole and fails.
- **S-03 money:** `₱`, `PHP`, and the word `peso` are removed, then the value is rounded half up to 2 decimals. A value of 10,000,000,000 or more is invalid.
- **S-05 names:** each word is capitalized and the rest lower-cased, so `juan DELA cruz` becomes `Juan Dela Cruz` and `JDC Hardware` becomes `Jdc Hardware`.
- **S-06 phone:** `0917-123-4567` becomes `09171234567`.

**Date ambiguity (S-01).** A slash date such as `03/04/2026` is read month first (March 4).

**Numeric precision and rounding.** Exact decimal arithmetic (Python `Decimal`), never floating point. Rounding is half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`) to 2 decimal places.

**Currency.** All money is Philippine peso. The currency is implicit and no currency column is stored.

### 4.2 Reference Values

| Column | Source variants | Standard value |
|---|---|---|
| `unit` | any casing, e.g. `PCS`, `Pcs` | `pcs` |
| `size` | any casing, e.g. `chb-4` | `CHB-4`. Hollow block sizes in use: `CHB-4`, `CHB-5`, `CHB-6`; other values are accepted and upper-cased |

No synonym mapping and no reference file are used in this version.

