## 5. Business Transformation Rules

### 5.1 Derived Columns, Lookups, and Filters

| Rule ID | Input columns | Logic or formula | Output column | Business reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| B-01 | `sales.quantity`, `sales.unit_price` | `total_amount = ROUND_HALF_UP(quantity * unit_price, 2)` using exact decimals, computed after cleaning | `sales.total_amount` DECIMAL(12,2) | Revenue per sale line. The source `total_amount` is never accepted; this is the only place it is created. |
| B-02 | none | No business exclusions. Every valid record is kept. | none | The business has no cancelled or excluded records, so the excluded count is 0 |

```text
total_amount = quantity x unit_price      (rounded half up to 2 decimals)
```

**Worked example (B-01)**

| Customer | `quantity` | `unit_price` | `total_amount` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Juan Dela Cruz | 100 | 12.51 | 1251.00 |
| Maria Santos | 50 | 1200.50 | 60025.00 |
| Pedro Reyes | 30 | 22.00 | 660.00 |

### 5.2 Rules That Do Not Apply (stated explicitly)

| Topic | Decision | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Joins | None. Parent keys are only looked up (read-only) to check referential integrity (C-08, V-06); no rows or columns are added. | No table needs to be combined in this stage |
| Aggregations | None | Output is at record level; daily totals or profit belong to the analytics layer |
| Business exclusions | None (B-02). The source has no status column. | The only removals are data-quality rejects (Section 3), each counted and logged |
| Dimensional modeling, surrogate keys, SCD | Not used. `blockflow.db` is an operational database with flat tables. | Avoids changing the Stage 1 model; no history tracking is required |

