| `updated_at` | `stocks.updated_at` | text | DATETIME | Standard date-time (S-01) |
| `recorded_by` | `stocks.recorded_by`, `sales.recorded_by`, `expenses.recorded_by` | text | INTEGER | Whole number (S-02), parent check (C-08) |
| `customer_name` | `sales.customer_name` | text | VARCHAR | Trim (C-01), fill (C-03), Title Case (S-05) |
| `phone_number` | `sales.phone_number` | text | VARCHAR | Digits only (S-06), fill (C-03) |
| `shop_name` | `sales.shop_name` | text | VARCHAR | Trim (C-01), fill (C-03), Title Case (S-05) |
| `sale_date` | `sales.sale_date` | text | DATETIME | Standard date-time (S-01) |
| `stock_id` | `sales.stock_id` | text | INTEGER | Whole number (S-02), required (C-05), parent check (C-08) |
| `quantity`, `unit_price` | `sales.total_amount` | text, text | DECIMAL(12,2) | Derived (B-01) |
| `category` | `expenses.category` | text | VARCHAR | Trim (C-01), Title Case (S-05) |
| `description` | `expenses.description` | text | TEXT | Trim (C-01), fill (C-04) |
| `amount` | `expenses.amount` | text | DECIMAL(12,2) | 2 decimals (S-03), above 0 (C-06) |
| `expense_date` | `expenses.expense_date` | text | DATETIME | Standard date-time (S-01) |

This contract describes what the Load stage receives. It differs from the extraction contract in the types (everything is typed), the derived `total_amount`, the placeholders for missing text, and the exclusion of rejected rows.

### 6.4 Schema Consistency

- A required column missing from the handover fails check V-01. The batch is REJECTED, nothing is transformed, and the mismatch is logged.
- A column outside the contract is dropped and logged, never mapped silently.
- A value that cannot be converted to its target type is never coerced; it is rejected under its S rule.
- A change to the contract is made in this document and in `transform.py` together, and the version number is raised before the pipeline is rerun.

