## 7. Transformation Validation and Data Quality Checks

The checks run inside the transformation task, after cleaning, on the transformed output. Extraction-stage checks (source connectivity, extraction execution, source-to-staging completeness) are not repeated. V-01 only confirms that the handover contains what this stage needs, and the extraction metadata is used as a reference for tracing and reconciliation.

| Check ID and name | Target | Purpose | Validation criteria | Severity |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| V-01 Input Handover | The package from Extraction | Make sure Transform has what it needs | Extraction status is APPROVED, all three DataFrames have the required columns, and the run metadata and validation summary are present | Critical |
| V-02 Record Reconciliation | Each output table | Detect lost records | `records_read = records_transformed + records_rejected` | Critical |
| V-03 Required Values Not Null | All NOT NULL columns | Ensure the output satisfies the contract | No null value in any column of Section 6 | Critical |
| V-04 Key Uniqueness | Each output table | Prevent duplicates | No repeated primary key, and no two records identical on the business columns | Critical |
| V-05 Data Type and Format Conformance | Each output table | Ensure the Load stage receives the contract types | Every column has its target type and format, and no extra or missing column | Critical |
| V-06 Referential Integrity | `recorded_by` and `sales.stock_id` | Prevent orphans | 100% of keys exist in the parent lookup. When the lookup is unavailable the check shows `SKIPPED` and is logged, and does not fail | Critical |
| V-07 Business Rules | Quantity, price, amount, `total_amount` | Ensure the business values make sense | Quantity, price, and amount are above 0; `total_amount` equals `quantity × unit_price` and is never negative | Critical |
| V-08 Aggregate Reconciliation | `quantity` (stocks, sales), `amount` (expenses) | Ensure no value was lost or changed | Sum of the measure in the input equals the sum in the output plus the sum in the rejected rows | Critical |
| V-09 Output Completeness | Each output table | Ensure the Load stage gets a complete day | Every table has at least 1 row after cleaning | Critical |
| V-10 Rejection Rate | Rejected rows per table | Catch an export fault or a mass entry error | Rejected rows are 5% or less of the table's input rows | Non-critical |

**Record reconciliation.** Rejected rows are the rows removed by C-05, C-06, C-08, or an S-rule failure, plus the duplicates rejected by C-07. A retained record that was cleaned or standardized is modified, not rejected, so `records_modified` is reported but is not part of the equation. No joins, aggregations, or exclusions exist in this stage, so there are no join, aggregation, or filter reconciliations.

**Timeout.** The 30-minute execution limit is enforced by Prefect. A timeout fails the run (REJECTED); it is not a data check.

