## 9. Log Retention, Rejected Data, and Access

Extraction and Transformation records are kept separately, even though both are stored on the same standalone PC as the pipeline and `blockflow.db`. Extraction logs record retrieval errors, extraction counts, and source-to-staging reconciliation. Transformation logs record cleaning actions, conversion errors, validation failures, and rejected records.

### 9.1 Storage and Retention

| Record | Location | Retention | Justification |
|---|---|---|---|
| Operational log (plain text) | `Pipeline/logs/transform_<timestamp>.log`, plus Prefect's own log storage | 12 months | Covers a full year of troubleshooting history, matching the Stage 1 aim of keeping a year easy to locate |
| Audit summary | `Pipeline/audit/transform_<timestamp>.json` | 24 months | The pipeline processes sales and financial data, so audit records are kept longer than operational logs |
| Quarantine (rejected records) | `Pipeline/rejected/transform_<timestamp>_<table>_rejected.csv`. This is separate from `entry/rejected/`, which holds whole failed batch files from extraction | 12 months | Long enough for the Owner to correct and re-extract the source and to answer questions from reports |

### 9.2 Quarantine Content

Each quarantine row keeps the original values plus `batch_id`, `rule_id`, and `rejection_reason`. A phone number is masked to its last 4 digits. Logs contain counts, rule IDs, and keys only, not full records, to avoid keeping unnecessary sensitive data.

### 9.3 Access Permissions

| Role | Read | Write | Delete |
|---|---|---|---|
| Owner | Yes | Yes | Yes, after the retention period |
| Staff | No | No | No |
| Pipeline run | No | Create only | No |

Staff record operational data but do not manage the pipeline, so access is restricted to prevent accidental changes. Access is enforced with operating-system file permissions on `logs/`, `audit/`, and `rejected/`, matching the standalone PC design.

### 9.4 Archiving and Deletion

- **Archiving:** at the start of each month, the previous month's logs, audit summaries, and quarantine files are compressed into one archive, verified as readable, and only then moved out of the active folders.
- **Deletion:** nothing is deleted before its retention period ends, and nothing is deleted while it is needed for troubleshooting, auditing, or recovery of an open batch. After the period, only the Owner deletes the expired archive, manually, and notes the deletion date. No automatic deletion exists.

