## 10. Transformation Acceptance and Handover Rules

Stage 1 decides whether data may proceed to Transformation. This stage decides whether the transformed output may proceed to Load.

### 10.1 Rejection-Rate Threshold

**5% of a table's input rows.** It is fixed in advance as the constant `REJECTION_RATE_LIMIT` and is not changed after seeing results.

*Justification:* the source is a manual log, so the odd bad row is expected, but a lost row changes sales and stock totals, so anything above 1 row in 20 needs the Owner's review. Because daily batches are small, one rejected row in a batch of fewer than 20 rows also triggers a review. A change to the threshold needs the Owner's approval and an update of this document.

### 10.2 Acceptance Rules

| Rule | Validation condition | Acceptance criteria | Pipeline action | Decision mode | Responsible person |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Automatic approval | Every critical check passes (or V-06 is skipped) and every table's rejection rate is within 5% | No FAIL and no WARNING | Mark the run APPROVED and hand over to Load | Automatic | None. The Prefect flow decides |
| Manual review | No critical check fails, but V-10 raises a WARNING | No FAIL, at least one WARNING | Hold the batch. Stage the transformed tables in `staging/` without handing them to Load. Notify the Owner through the run log and the audit summary | Manual | Owner, or Staff designated by the Owner, who reads the quarantine and either corrects the source and reruns, or reruns with `--accept-warnings` |
| Rejection | Any critical check fails (V-01 to V-09), or the task fails after 3 retries or exceeds the 30-minute timeout | One or more critical FAIL | Stop the handover and do not start Load. Retry only transient task faults (3 times). Keep the rejected rows in the quarantine. Mark the run REJECTED | Automatic at detection | Owner decides when the source is fixed and the batch is rerun |
| Handover | The run is APPROVED (automatically, or by the Owner accepting warnings) | No unresolved FAIL | Pass the three items in 10.3 to Load | Automatic once approved | None |

### 10.3 Handover to Load

The following is passed on, and the metadata and validation summary are also written to the `audit/` folder as the run's permanent record:

1. The transformed DataFrames for `stocks`, `sales`, and `expenses`, in the Section 6 contract.
2. The run metadata: `run_id`, `parent_run_id`, `batch_id`, counts per table, and `rules_applied`.
3. The validation summary.

### 10.4 Decision Rules

| Overall condition | Acceptance decision | Pipeline action |
|---|---|---|
| All tables PASS | APPROVED | Proceed to Load |
| One or more non-critical WARNING | MANUAL REVIEW | Hold batch |
| One or more critical FAIL | REJECTED | Stop, retry transient faults, quarantine rejected rows |

**Example validation summary** (the seeded test batch of Section 2)

| Validation summary | Result |
|---|---|
| stocks transformation | WARNING (5 of 7 rows rejected) |
| sales transformation | WARNING (3 of 6 rows rejected) |
| expenses transformation | WARNING (1 of 4 rows rejected) |
| Overall Transformation | MANUAL REVIEW |

