## 11. Common Transformation Problems and Mitigation

| Problem | Possible cause | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Duplicate records after a rerun | The same batch is run again | Inflated sales and stock totals | The stage is idempotent and writes no data, so a rerun yields the same output. C-07 and V-04 remove and detect duplicates inside a batch. The Load stage's UPSERT protects the database |
| Late-arriving records | A record for a closed day is entered after the 12:00 AM run | The day's report is missing a record | Rerun that day with `--date`. The rerun is safe, and `batch_id` shows which day was reprocessed |
| Unexpected schema change | The export renames, drops, or adds a column | Wrong mapping or failure | V-01 rejects a batch with a missing required column. Extra columns are dropped and logged. The contract and `transform_version` are updated together before rerunning |
| Ambiguous date format | `03/04/2026` can be March 4 or April 3 | A record is stored on the wrong day | Dates are read month first and standardized to one format. The Owner should keep one export format. A date outside the batch window shows up in the sales reports and can be corrected at the source and rerun |
| Orphan foreign keys | A `recorded_by` or `stock_id` that does not exist in the database | The Load stage would reject the row or the link would break | C-08 rejects the row to quarantine and V-06 confirms none remain |
| Parent lookup unavailable | `blockflow.db` missing, locked, or not yet created | Orphans cannot be detected here | V-06 shows SKIPPED and is logged. The Load stage's foreign key constraints are the final guard |
| Too many rows rejected | An export fault, a changed column format, or a mass entry error | An incomplete day reaches the database | V-10 raises a WARNING above 5% and holds the batch for Owner review |
| Transformation exceeds its time window | Data volume growth | The daily run does not finish before the next day | The 30-minute task timeout fails the run (REJECTED), nothing is handed to Load, and the batch is rerun. If volume grows, tables can be processed in chunks |
| Sensitive data kept in quarantine | Rejected rows copy customer details | Unnecessary exposure of phone numbers | Phone numbers are masked to the last 4 digits and the folder is restricted to the Owner |

Row multiplication after a join does not apply, because this stage joins no tables. V-02, V-04, and V-08 would detect it if a join is added later.
